### Gmail Integration API Tests
### Test real email sending through the Pet Care Service API

@baseUrl = https://localhost:8443/api
@testEmail = your.real.email@gmail.com
@testPassword = TestPass123

### 1. Test Email Verification (Registration Flow)
# This will send a real verification email if Gmail is configured
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/start-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "Gmail Test User",
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": "{{testPassword}}",
    "gender": "Male",
    "role": "Pet owner",
    "city": "Test City",
    "address": "123 Test Street"
}

### 2. Test Password Reset Email
# This will send a real password reset email if Gmail is configured
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{testEmail}}"
}

### 3. Test Email Verification for Existing User
# First, you need to login to get a token from a previous registration
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 4. Resend Email Verification (requires auth token from login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/resend-email-verification
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

### Expected Results with Gmail Configured:
# ✅ Real emails sent to your Gmail inbox
# ✅ Console logs show "Gmail SMTP connection verified"  
# ✅ Console logs show "Email verification sent: [MESSAGE_ID]"
# ✅ You'll receive actual emails with verification codes

### Expected Results without Gmail (Development Mode):
# 📝 Emails logged to console only
# 📝 Console shows "Using development mode - emails will be logged to console"
# 📝 No real emails sent, but codes displayed in server logs

### To Enable Gmail:
# 1. Uncomment these lines in .env:
#    GMAIL_EMAIL=your.email@gmail.com
#    GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=your_16_digit_app_password
# 2. Replace with your actual Gmail credentials
# 3. Restart the server
# 4. Run these tests again
